1
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble,
and even my shoes flew off.

3
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:32,920
onto the head of the carpenter
I had put in a chokehold,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
Katsushika, one more yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,180
the town feels strangely kind.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat,
from the water canteen,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset falls into the great sky.

10
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:15,920
Why does tomorrow have to end too?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,020
Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness is lost.

12
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,680
I listened and realized,
because I'm such a fool.

13
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:31,580
Wild fantasies, outrageous new inventions!

14
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:50,580
Wow, there are so many people!

15
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:52,860
As expected of the motor festival, isn't it?

16
00:01:55,680 --> 00:02:01,840
Who on earth came here, I wonder? This world may not be much of a connection for Ryo-chan,
since he doesn't have a car.

17
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:10,300
I have cars too, you know! A Countach, a Mustang, a King Tiger tank...
those are all model kits, aren't they?

18
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,160
Anyway, let's go inside.

19
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:41,000
You're making sure they get
our faces on camera, right?

20
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:45,400
These people really do pop up from everywhere,
don't they.

21
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:46,460
Honestly.

22
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:48,980
What on earth are they here for?

23
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:54,380
Stop!

24
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:57,760
Aaaaaah!

25
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:01,100
Aaaaaah! What're you going on about!

26
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:05,780
What a terrible driver! No way...

27
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:20,740
Yeah, I did it! I've got the scent of art, a man who knows the difference!
Esaki, I'll kill you, Professor Esaki!

28
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:22,840
Showing up and causing a commotion again.

29
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,980
Bonjour, Monsieur Nakagawa.

30
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:28,260
How are you feeling today?

31
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:29,540
Mademoiselle Reiko.

32
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:33,620
You knock people flying, then call
yourself a man who knows the difference?

33
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:36,260
Aren't you a mountain gorilla?

34
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:37,900
Who's a gorilla?

35
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:39,280
Then Peking Man.

36
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:39,960
No.

37
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:42,200
I'm Japanese.

38
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:46,120
It's a witty French joke.

39
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:46,960
Do you know?

40
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:49,720
Cro-Magnon Man,
the ancestor of modern humans,

41
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:53,280
was discovered in southern France in 1868.

42
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:57,020
France truly is the land of history and art!

43
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:58,660
Way too intense.

44
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,779
What? The genuine great
thief born in France,

45
00:04:05,829 --> 00:04:07,540
Arsène Lupin!

46
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:08,755
Lupin?

47
00:04:08,805 --> 00:04:12,180
in the flower-blooming Edo, there was
the great thief called Nezumi Kozō...

48
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,200
What the hell are you doing?

49
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:16,900
It's not the vulgar pronunciation "Rupan,"

50
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:18,480
it's "Lupin," Lupin!

51
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,360
That's French bread, isn't it?

52
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:23,780
In France,
they even use this bread for pedigree.

53
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:25,380
That's ridiculous.

54
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,180
Anyway, Nakagawa-kun, Miss,

55
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:31,520
are you two still driving
Ferraris and Porsches?

56
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,400
Y-yes, well,

57
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,020
yes.

58
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,760
Tsk, you should switch to French cars.

59
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:38,340
Citroën, Renault, Peugeot.

60
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:41,300
French cars have love and art.

61
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:46,050
That's not right.
You went on about Jaguars and afternoon tea,

62
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:48,900
and you were completely
besotted with England.

63
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:53,320
Non, non. France is the country
overflowing with the scent of Europe.

64
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:55,440
Professor, when did you come to France?

65
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:58,960
I've been teaching at the
Sorbonne for two weeks now.

66
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:02,000
Two weeks and you've already
gone completely French?

67
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:05,100
Even now, the sound of the
Seine's current won't leave my ears.

68
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:08,741
That place where painters
from all over the world gather,

69
00:05:08,791 --> 00:05:10,800
the slopes of Montmartre hill.

70
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:14,160
Ahhhhhh

71
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,540
Eeeeeeee

72
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,760
Ahhhhhh

73
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:22,180
Mm-hmm

74
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:30,980
And I was in the fencing club, with all these...
still, zero...

75
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:37,640
Anyway, you probably drove down the stairs and crashed into a shop,
then pulled your usual cover-up, didn't you?

76
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:39,840
Senpai, please stop.

77
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,540
Like the other day, again.

78
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:43,460
If it turns into a duel,
it'll be a disaster.

79
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:44,560
They're waiting, you know.

80
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:46,660
I don't even feel like competing anymore.

81
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:47,620
It's just too ridiculous.

82
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:49,280
By the way, Professor.

83
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:51,280
Who sent this invitation?

84
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,760
Wimsch, exactly.

85
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,860
I invited you all.

86
00:05:55,860 --> 00:05:59,540
My invention is also entered in this year's award,
you see.

87
00:06:00,340 --> 00:06:02,200
Even so, you know.

88
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:02,500
It's just habit.

89
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:07,980
What the hell was that?

90
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:14,620
Ladies and gentlemen, the 21st
century is truly the age of the tank!

91
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:18,180
That's why I have developed
a revolutionary tank machine

92
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:20,300
called the Fully Automatic-kun.

93
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:24,560
Isn't that just a joke, slapping tank
caterpillar treads onto a tank machine?

94
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,080
You there!

95
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:30,300
Do you know why Napoleon invaded Russia?

96
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:31,920
As if I'd cut it, you idiot!

97
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:32,380
There wasn't any!

98
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:35,000
Then keep quiet, amateur!

99
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:37,940
Even if it doesn't look like it,
this is no ordinary car wash machine!

100
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:40,360
It identifies the car
model with the lens on top,

101
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:43,180
analyzes the car's dirt with a computer,

102
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:47,600
and sprays water and special cleaning fluid
from 50 spots to remove dirt from every detail!

103
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:48,820
And on top of that!

104
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:51,220
It can go anywhere on caterpillar treads!

105
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:53,920
In short, this robot, Senjuu-kun,

106
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:56,840
is, so to speak,
a mobile car wash machine with a brain!

107
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:06,000
So it moves on its own, and all you have to do
is park and it finishes the car wash for you?

108
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,220
Does it really work that well?

109
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:10,780
Then let me demonstrate right away.

110
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:16,420
Fully Automatic Kun Car Wash Course,
starting up!

111
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:21,740
Power on. Identifying the
vehicle type and starting the wash.

112
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:26,380
Then all you have to do
is relax and smoke a pipe.

113
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,040
Crash!

114
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:31,140
The soft top!

115
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:32,900
Now it's basically a convertible.

116
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:35,020
I forgot to engage the soft top stopper.

117
00:07:35,020 --> 00:07:38,540
Search complete. Washing, washing.

118
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,240
Let's go, time-out!

119
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:45,080
Starting cleaning fluid release.

120
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:46,540
H-help!

121
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,000
Bebbe's -

122
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,580
Down, down, down!

123
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:56,520
What a miserable sight.

124
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,840
This is no time to be
saying things like that!

125
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,840
We have to save him quickly,
or it'll be a disaster!

126
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:05,240
Operation complete. Operation complete.

127
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,320
Hey, mister, are you all right?

128
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:11,280
The detergent has dissolved in,
and I can't see inside well.

129
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,020
I wonder if he's okay.

130
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,420
Sipping café au lait
on the terrace like this

131
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:29,540
is the Parisian's moment of rest.

132
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,960
What moment of rest? You're soaking wet!

133
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,480
You just don't get it.

134
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:39,940
I was showing you how it cleans the
interior and clothes at the same time.

135
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:43,820
You're spouting nonsense again,
you bucket-hater!

136
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:47,440
Under the Paris sky, the Seine flows on,

137
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:50,500
and that chanson I heard on the Champs-Élysées was
"Autumn Leaves."

138
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,720
You bastard!

139
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:52,940
Aaah!

140
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:53,920
S-senpai!

141
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:55,860
Woohoo!

142
00:08:56,240 --> 00:09:02,380
Academic analysis started!
Search complete! Beginning operation!

143
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:06,120
Ah ah, let go! Hey!

144
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:06,740
Nyaa!

145
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:08,520
Senpai!

146
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:09,300
Yosh!

147
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,600
Woohoo!

148
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:11,640
Stop it!

149
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:12,620
Yaa!

150
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:16,480
Professor!
Hurry and turn it off with the remote!

151
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:18,960
This one.

152
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,220
Hey, looks like it's broken.

153
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:27,980
No way, so the fully automatic one is

154
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:30,240
moving on its own!

155
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:34,560
No need to be alarmed,
that's what makes it amazing!

156
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:38,860
Water wash complete.

157
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:39,820
Shishina

158
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:40,980
Gas scrub started.

159
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,620
Gas scrub started.

160
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:45,140
So it can't be stopped, right?

161
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:45,900
Should we go?

162
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:49,660
Shurupuru?

163
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:53,120
Work complete! Work complete!

164
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:53,600
Hey!

165
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:56,340
Ryo-chan!

166
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:57,380
S-senpai!

167
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:01,320
Eww! Ryo-chan's all shiny!

168
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:04,160
I didn't become like this by choice!

169
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,780
Well! It's moving again!

170
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:32,940
!

171
00:10:37,940 --> 00:10:39,400
Everyone, what's wrong?

172
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:42,680
I'm just too beautiful.

173
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:47,020
Anytime, anywhere,
twinkle, twinkle, twinkle.

174
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:53,180
Those who can't bear to be without me...

175
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:56,540
Leave it to me, Ichisenshi!

176
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:58,460
He's completely getting carried away.

177
00:10:58,460 --> 00:11:00,380
Guess we'll have to cut the power.

178
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,040
Ryo-chan!

179
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:03,940
Get up!

180
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,280
Yah!

181
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:06,620
It's coming straight at us!

182
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:08,940
It jumped on nicely!

183
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:10,860
It's probably pointless.

184
00:11:11,180 --> 00:11:14,940
Senjiro-kun has a
self-defense system installed.

185
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,860
Why would you install something like that?

186
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:21,401
In this day and age, even machines

187
00:11:21,451 --> 00:11:23,940
must protect themselves.

188
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,740
Where's the remote?

189
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:27,620
Damn it!

190
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,620
You're letting go?

191
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:30,780
Whoa!

192
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:33,260
Ugh, haa, no way!

193
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:43,820
It's resisting.

194
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:47,400
Mee-mee-mee, genius!

195
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:51,980
-Senpai!-Ryo-chan!

196
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:54,420
Yes, what a despicable bastard!

197
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,560
It was a perfect defense system, wasn't it?

198
00:11:57,820 --> 00:12:00,100
Hey, stop bragging and
do something about it!

199
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,660
The whole car wash has
moved to another stage!

200
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:17,040
It wrecked the car!

201
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:20,020
Looks like it's washing
the car on super hard mode.

202
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:22,380
That's not washing, it's destruction!
Stop it now!

203
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:26,420
My fully automatic car is
a professional car washer!

204
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:30,640
Now it won't stop for anyone until
every car in the venue is washed.

205
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,080
I'm telling you, it's destruction!

206
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:34,400
Washing, washing!

207
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:38,400
Hey, it's spraying water!

208
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:40,780
Looks like it plans to wash the whole venue.

209
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:42,340
"Looks like" isn't good enough!

210
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:45,560
At this rate,
the waterfront will be completely soaked!

211
00:12:47,460 --> 00:12:50,700
Wash, wash, washing, wash!

212
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:52,560
Do something!

213
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:53,640
Professor!

214
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:55,160
Where the hell did that thing go!

215
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:59,820
Wash it, wash it, wash it, wash!

216
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:10,000
Car wash complete,

217
00:13:10,050 --> 00:13:12,080
Car wash complete.

218
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:25,560
Well, this really made a spectacular mess,
didn't it.

219
00:13:27,620 --> 00:13:34,840
That bastard.

220
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:36,380
How about that?

221
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:39,300
I did equip it with a self-destruct
search function for just such an occasion.

222
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:41,060
It just broke down on its own, didn't it.

223
00:13:57,100 --> 00:14:00,520
There's not a single dangerous
thing in my inventions.

224
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:03,220
Aren't you the most dangerous person here?

225
00:14:03,740 --> 00:14:04,140
Yeah.

226
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:07,740
There's another invention
left in the second venue.

227
00:14:08,340 --> 00:14:10,560
Hey, Reiko.

228
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:14,600
Let's go! If we keep getting dragged into this,
we'll die a dozen times over!

229
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:16,160
Senpai!

230
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:19,840
That's too bad.
It's a new virtual game, though.

231
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:23,720
A new virtual game, you say?

232
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,800
Then Gorilla-kun won't mind, will he? Miss.

233
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:32,700
Wait! If it's a game, that's a different story.
Let me play too!

234
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:35,640
Bingo! This one!

235
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:39,200
"Bingo, this one," you said. Just this one?

236
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:45,020
But you can't play a game
without a car and a screen!

237
00:14:45,020 --> 00:14:46,320
Don't worry, it's all set up.

238
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:49,000
Just put on the helmet and see.

239
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:52,100
The helmet doesn't look dangerous, though.

240
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:54,300
Grip the steering wheel.

241
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:56,760
What? What's going on?

242
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:00,520
There's a screen inside the visor!

243
00:15:00,940 --> 00:15:03,440
Now tilt the steering wheel forward.

244
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:04,400
Here?

245
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:06,480
We're moving!

246
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:08,620
Amazing.

247
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:12,260
Amazing!
So this helmet doubles as VR goggles!

248
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:18,440
Impressive! This is the only
compact VR driving game in the world!

249
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:21,680
It's called "Engine Full-Throttle Blast!"

250
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:27,720
It even has built-in stereo headphones.
It's just like the real thing!

251
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:30,340
This is quite something...

252
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:34,060
Simulation development is the professor's specialty,
after all!

253
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:37,800
Then show us a demonstration right away!

254
00:15:38,620 --> 00:15:39,240
A demo.

255
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:41,540
Come on, come on, hurry up!

256
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:42,580
W-what, what?

257
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:43,520
Come on, come on, come on!

258
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,420
A hairpin turn right away!

259
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:59,740
Th-this, this, the, the...
ulp, the racing line!

260
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:03,720
The movement is creepy.

261
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:07,360
Doesn't it look like someone wearing
a Walkman and doing the bubble dance?

262
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:14,500
I don't know what's going on,
but it's really intense.

263
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:26,220
See? By the fourth lap,
your lap times have improved!

264
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,660
From the outside,
nobody can tell what's happening!

265
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:30,900
This is fine, isn't it?

266
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:34,400
If you connect the lines,
six people can race at the same time!

267
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,180
Don't bring your sweaty face so close!

268
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,840
When they line up, it's amazing.

269
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,740
It feels kind of dangerous, doesn't it?

270
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:45,680
Here we go!

271
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:46,340
GO!

272
00:16:55,940 --> 00:16:58,600
They don't look like they're racing at all.

273
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,800
No matter how you look at it,
they're a bunch of perverts.

274
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,920
Isn't it amazing?

275
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:12,640
It sounds fun, but from the outside they just look like dangerous people in the buff.
That's a problem.

276
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:14,920
There's no car body, after all.

277
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:19,460
Good eye, Nakagawa.

278
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:21,480
Anyone would notice that.

279
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:25,140
That's why I developed this.

280
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:33,520
F1 machines,

281
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:34,480
two of them.

282
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:37,320
Is this the real thing?

283
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:38,680
Of course.

284
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:42,200
The man who insists on the real thing,
Esaki Satsuke.

285
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:44,780
Engine Bari-Bari Zenkai-kun

286
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:46,980
by joining it to a real F1 machine,

287
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:49,380
we achieve the ultimate virtual reality.

288
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:52,600
Step on the gas and the
virtual image speeds up, too.

289
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:56,380
If you spin out or crash,
you'll be flung right out of the car!

290
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:03,240
So the only ones who can ride this
perfectly are real F1 racers or me.

291
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:05,960
Well then, let's race, you and me.

292
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:09,580
You'd better not.

293
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:13,720
People used to say I was as good
as Schumacher or Ezaki Korosuke.

294
00:18:14,080 --> 00:18:16,040
You two won't stand a chance against me.

295
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:21,060
After all, I played that driving
game that came out in the Showa 30s,

296
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:27,720
the man who conquered the Tokyo-Osaka route.

297
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:32,720
If you're going to quit, now's the time.

298
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:34,520
When I say it's a contest, it's a contest.

299
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:37,100
Speaking of which,
what about the tire temperature?

300
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:38,680
Getting scared?

301
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:41,380
I'll leave a lowly racer
like you in the dust.

302
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,920
You two really hate losing, don't you?

303
00:18:54,660 --> 00:18:55,800
Charging out of nowhere!

304
00:18:58,080 --> 00:18:59,200
It's so intense!

305
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:06,160
What kind of driving is this?

306
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:08,660
Didn't it crash into the audience seats?

307
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:11,540
It might have killed four or five people.

308
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,480
The sense of speed is incredible!

309
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:16,260
Alright,
we'll pull ahead on this straightaway!

310
00:19:24,100 --> 00:19:25,440
It really started moving!

311
00:19:29,700 --> 00:19:30,580
It's virtual, baby!

312
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:32,620
Leave it to me!

313
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:37,660
Both of them haven't
noticed because of Zenkai-kun!

314
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:38,800
Let's go after them!

315
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:16,740
It's getting crowded!

316
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:19,280
A red light!

317
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:23,140
Whoa! High-speed F2 corner!

318
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:29,120
Why am I feeling uneasy?

319
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:34,720
So...

320
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:40,660
High-speed corner!

321
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:41,460
No way!

322
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:49,800
This is bad for my heart.
How long is this going to last?

323
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:53,660
Maybe if it's game over
or the battery runs out...

324
00:20:53,660 --> 00:20:56,100
Now it's a railroad crossing!

325
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,620
Another high-speed curve!

326
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:06,000
Go! We've landed in a sand trap!

327
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:13,140
The crossing barrier was down, you know!

328
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,540
Oh no! A train is coming!

329
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,200
That's divine skill!

330
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:27,360
Both of you,
that's a technique only possible in a game!

331
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:31,140
Ugh

332
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:32,120
What!

333
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:32,940
Hey!

334
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:33,780
Zukoryō!

335
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:35,420
Whoa!

336
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:36,100
Hmm

337
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:38,520
By my calculations,
we're almost at the finish line!

338
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:39,840
This is a showdown!

339
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:41,960
I won't let you pass!

340
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:44,120
Wow, that's amazing!

341
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:45,560
Looks like it's super fast!

342
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:46,680
We're leaving them all behind!

343
00:21:49,860 --> 00:21:51,100
W-what was that just now?

344
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:52,640
W-well...

345
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,900
Uh-oh, we've entered the racetrack!

346
00:22:07,140 --> 00:22:10,140
Now the horses have rounded the fourth
corner and entered the final straight!

347
00:22:10,140 --> 00:22:11,100
Leading the pack is...

348
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:14,420
It's an F1! Two F1 machines are running!

349
00:22:14,420 --> 00:22:15,960
What on earth just happened?

350
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:16,800
This is...

351
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:19,860
It's still running!

352
00:22:19,860 --> 00:22:21,600
What's going to happen?

353
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:25,780
That cheering is incredible.
Is the finish line close?

354
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:27,964
Whoa,

355
00:22:28,014 --> 00:22:31,640
What amazing virtual reality!
Horses are running around the racetrack!

356
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:35,280
Ha how about that? Pretty amazing, right?

357
00:22:35,620 --> 00:22:36,939
Wait,

358
00:22:36,989 --> 00:22:39,900
I don't remember making this simulation...

359
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:42,280
Whoever reaches the goal first, trip them!

360
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:44,460
I won't let that happen!

361
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,560
Aaaaaah!

362
00:23:02,940 --> 00:23:06,240
I won! What are you talking about? I won!

363
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:12,700
Aaaaaah!

364
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,560
Up to here, at least...

365
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:26,120
What's going on? The game ended,
but we're still at the racetrack!

366
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:30,500
Hey, this isn't virtual!

367
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:33,580
The two of them went
back to reality, though.

368
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:35,940
The spectators have started a riot.

369
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:40,860
Virtual beyond virtual.
This sense of reality is...

370
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:43,620
Reality my ass, it's all the real deal!

371
00:23:45,180 --> 00:23:48,080
Oh no, my presentation at the
New York conference is starting!

372
00:23:48,820 --> 00:23:50,020
Well then, I'll be going.

373
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:52,380
Dan! H-hey! Don't run away!

374
00:23:53,860 --> 00:23:55,980
That was dangerous, Silvaplat!

375
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:07,360
What's that gyoza-looking flower, Chief?

376
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:10,120
Is this flower really that expensive?

377
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:13,560
Alright, I can grow flowers too!

378
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:16,820
Even if Pochi whines in the back field,
I'm rolling in money!

379
00:24:17,980 --> 00:24:21,320
Next time: Funtō Harasaka Dormitory,
see you!

380
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:44,000
Solved by sheer spirit, swiftly erased

381
00:24:44,540 --> 00:24:45,760
Prediction

382
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:49,900
Decided, then a flash of inspiration

383
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:52,740
Bouncing along, all wrapped up

384
00:24:52,740 --> 00:24:55,720
Into action, soaring away

385
00:24:56,640 --> 00:25:00,420
Above all, Smoney Power

386
00:25:00,420 --> 00:25:06,360
Everyone gather, come here

387
00:25:07,260 --> 00:25:12,720
The dreamlike final energy

388
00:25:13,840 --> 00:25:17,140
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday

389
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:20,020
Painting the universe,
standing on the ground

390
00:25:20,020 --> 00:25:23,840
Kameari's star spun round in a circle

391
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:27,500
This should be fine, right?

392
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:28,940
Like hell it is!

393
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,800
Thank you for watching.

